.TH SUBX 1 "August 2026" "SubX 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
subx \- Asynchronous Subdomain Reconnaissance & Asset Management Framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B subx
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SubX is a fast, asynchronous attack-surface mapping and subdomain enumeration tool designed for security researchers, penetration testers, and bug bounty hunters.
It aggregates reconnaissance findings from multiple passive sources (like Shodan, VirusTotal, Censys, and ProjectDiscovery Chaos), filters results against custom target scopes, and manages asset lifecycles inside a SQLite or PostgreSQL database.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fbenum\fR
Enumerate subdomains for target domains defined in a YAML/JSON configuration file.
.TP
\fbhttp-probe\fR
Probe stored subdomains for HTTP liveness, response status codes, HTML titles, and web technology stacks using httpx.
.TP
\fbdb\fR
Query, filter, export, or manage stored subdomains in the database.
.TP
\fbproject\fR
Export a structured plain-text recon directory layout per target domain.
.TP
\fbimport-sqlite\fR
Import an existing SQLite database into PostgreSQL or active target database engine.
.TP
\fbdev-migrate\fR
Migrate database schema when upgrading database models.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR
Path to YAML/JSON scope and API keys configuration file.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-domain\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR
Target domain name.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-project\fR
Export plain-text project folder structure after scan.
.SH AUTHOR
